Rowan was a small, fine-boned man with a blue and green gem set into his throat. He was an enemy of [[Org/Althane/The Weft|the Weft]], who killed him, and he came back. What returned wore his shape only at first: it became a mass of mouths, eyes and arms, and it blamed the Weft for his death.

He ran errands for [[People/Althane/The Broker|T3C]], who handed him the artifacts that saw [[People/Althane/Divex|Divex]] blamed for their theft, and he put them away in a storehouse. When T3C was shot, no one came back for them. Rowan set the gem in his throat and became the thing the Weft met, and he served [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]] in his last fight, shielded by a giant sword that hung in the air. When the Feep died the Weft killed Rowan too; the burst of force that tore the weave where he stood would have consumed him, but a blue portal opened under him first and he was pulled away through it.

Rowan was blessed by the Feep. Earlier, in a fight between Oresk's [[Org/Althane/The First House|First House]], Rowan and the Weft at the Night Market, Rowan exploded, vaporising [[People/Althane/Big Fish|Big Fish]] and throwing the rest of the Weft into a branch reality.

Rowan was being shunted, pseudo-randomly, backward in time and space by his patron, [[Divinity/Althane/The Stranger|the Feep]], so the Weft had met him a handful of times before he met them. They found him again in the annex of the Arcanum in Illyara and travelled with him a while, then, fearing he would betray them, betrayed and killed him first; he resurrected and teleported away.
